        "description": "Most companies are not failing with AI because the tools are weak.\nThey’re failing because they’re low clarity and high noise.\n\nThis video breaks down a simple 2x2 framework to diagnose why AI efforts stall and what to fix first.\n\nWhat you’ll learn:\n\nThe 2 variables that determine AI leverage\nThe 4 quadrants companies fall into\nThe path from chaos to scale\nIf your team feels busy but not compounding, this model will help you decide the right next move: more clarity or more leverage.\n\n*2x2 Operator Grid Audit*\nUse this to diagnose one company function.\n\n*Step 1: Pick The Function*\nFunction:\nOwner:\nTeam size:\n\n*Step 2: Score Clarity*\nDo we know what great looks like?\nDo we have driver metrics?\nDo we have documented processes?\nDo we have clear ownership?\n\n*Step 3: Score Leverage*\nIs AI used only ad hoc?\nAre there repeatable workflows?\nAre outputs consistent?\nAre any lanes partially autonomous?\n\n*Step 4: Plot The Function*\nStuck = low clarity, low leverage\nCraft = high clarity, low leverage\nNoise = low clarity, high leverage\nScale = high clarity, high leverage\n\n*Step 5: Decide The Next Move*\nWhat needs clarity first?\nWhat should be AI-enabled now?\nWhat should not be automated yet?\n\n#AI #AIOperations #BusinessStrategy #Automation #leadership \n\n00:00 Why companies fail with AI\n00:10 Low clarity, high noise\n00:14 The 2x2 model\n00:30 Clarity\n00:43 Leverage\n00:59 Four quadrants\n01:08 Move between quadrants\n01:50 Path to scale\n02:04 Your next move",
